# The names of the values this app reads. Never put a real value in this file.
#
# On WebDIY there is nothing to set: when the project's database is turned on,
# the public VITE_NEON_* addresses arrive in `.env` and the secrets below reach
# the Worker as bindings when the dev server starts.
#
# Outside WebDIY: put the VITE_NEON_* addresses in `.env` (they are public) and
# the secrets in `.dev.vars` (kept out of git), then `wrangler secret put` each
# secret before the first deploy.

# --- Public (.env) ---------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=
# VITE_NEON_JWKS_URL=
# VITE_NEON_DATA_API_URL=

# --- Secrets (.dev.vars locally, `wrangler secret put` when deployed) -------
# Signs the auth proxy's session cache cookie: any random value of 32 or more
# characters (for example `openssl rand -base64 32`).
# NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET=
# The database's connection string for server routes (the app_rw role).
# DATABASE_URL=
